Anand,

RFI-007 response.

RECOMMENDATION: **Option 2 — found the footing at 2.4m depth on the hard rock with redesign.**

JUSTIFICATION:
1. Hard granite has much higher SBC (1,800-2,400 kN/m²) than the design SBC of 480 kN/m². There is no engineering reason to go deeper.
2. The footing can be reduced in size — see attached calculation.
3. F-18 redesign attached.

REDESIGN SUMMARY (F-18 only):
- Original footing: 3.0 × 3.0 × 0.6 m at 3.8m depth (RCC M35 + 184 kg rebar)
- Revised footing: 1.8 × 1.8 × 0.5 m at 2.4m depth (RCC M35 + 84 kg rebar)
- Cost saving: ~INR 1.4 lakh per footing
- Schedule: SAVES 1 day

ALERT: Check adjacent footings F-17, F-19, F-25. If similar rock at 2.4m, similar redesign applies. We may need a localised geotech re-test if more than 4 footings show rock at < 3m depth.

I will issue a formal "Drawing Revision" to F-18 footing detail by 14:00 IST tomorrow. Until then, proceed with caution — do not commit any concrete in F-18 until you have the revised drawing.

Best,
